    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows sustained positive bias (e.g., multiple 0.50 values) as market may overreact.",
    "Reduce forecast volatility after sharp price spikes; model tends to overshoot post-spikes.",
    "Apply mean reversion correction if forecast deviates >15% from 15-day moving average of true outcomes.",
    "Increase forecast lag sensitivity when sentiment history includes negative values (e.g., -0.25) to avoid premature reactions.",
    "Lower forecast peaks when sentiment history shows recent upward momentum (e.g., consecutive 0.00 values) to prevent overconfidence.",
    "Apply downward bias correction if model consistently overpredicts in low-sentiment periods (e.g., sentiment < 0.00)."
